### 3.8 Baselines Study

#### Poisson Baseline

Assuming kaon and anti-kaon are independent distributed as Poisson distribution. The difference of two independent Poisson distributions distributed as the Skellam distributions. It's probability density formula is:

\[P(N)=(\frac{\mu_{1}}{\mu_{2}})^{(}N/2)I_{N}(2\sqrt{\mu_{1}\mu_{2}})e^{-(\mu_{1} +\mu_{2})} \tag{3.20}\]

, where the \(\mu_{1}\) and \(\mu_{2}\) are the mean value of two Poisson distributions, respectively, the \(I_{k}(z)\) is the modified bessel function of the first kind. Then the net-kaon distribution can be expressed as skellam distribution. Then the expectation of the various cumulants (\(C_{1},C_{2},C_{3},C_{4}\)) and moment products (\(\sigma^{2}\)/M, S\(\sigma\), \(\kappa\sigma^{2}\)) can be

